    "comment": "The fired side of porcelain. Every companion blocktype gets the colour too, not just the headline vessel: bowl-meal or a filled porcelain bowl fails to resolve when you eat from it, dirtypot or a used porcelain cooking pot has nowhere to go, and oillamp-empty is where the raw genie lamp actually fires to. dirtypot's texturesByType ends in a '*' catch-all that would claim porcelain first \u2014 ClayByTypeOrderFix moves it back to last at load, which is where vanilla's own convention says it belongs.",
