  {
    "comment": "The porcelain payoff, and the reason to want it beyond looks. Vanilla reads spoilSpeedMulByFoodCat and transitionSpeedMul off the block for a BlockEntityGenericTypedContainer and renders the 'Stored food perish speed' line itself, so this needs no code at all. Vanilla's own vessel is vegetable 0.75 / grain 0.5; the values here merge over those. The crock is not eligible \u2014 BlockCrock hardcodes its 0.85/0.25/0.1 multipliers with no JSON exposure.",
    "file": "game:blocktypes/clay/fired/storagevessel",
    "op": "addmerge",
    "path": "/attributesByType",
    "value": {
      "*-porcelain-*": {
        "spoilSpeedMulByFoodCat": {
          "normal": {
            "vegetable": 0.5,
            "grain": 0.3,
            "fruit": 0.6,
            "dairy": 0.6,
            "protein": 0.75
          }
        },
        "transitionSpeedMul": {
          "normal": {
            "Perish": 0.6
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
]
